    💭 Strings
    🔡 check 🔤plain text is quoted🔤 🧼🐇🧾 🔤Ship it🔤❗️ 🔤"Ship it"🔤❗️
    🔡 check 🔤an empty string is two quotes🔤 🧼🐇🧾 🔤🔤❗️ 🔤""🔤❗️
    🔡 check 🔤a quote is escaped🔤 🧼🐇🧾 🔤say "hi"🔤❗️ 🔤"say \"hi\""🔤❗️
    🔡 check 🔤a backslash is escaped🔤 🧼🐇🧾 🔤a\b🔤❗️ 🔤"a\\b"🔤❗️
    🔡 check 🔤line breaks and tabs get their short escapes🔤 🧼🐇🧾 🔤a❌nb❌rc❌td🔤❗️ 🔤"a\nb\rc\td"🔤❗️
    🔡 check 🔤text beyond ASCII is left as it is🔤 🧼🐇🧾 🔤café 🍇🔤❗️ 🔤"café 🍇"🔤❗️
    💭 The decoder turns escapes into the raw characters, which is how a request can put them in a path.
    🆕📨 🔤GET🔤 🔤/%01%1F🔤❗️ ➡️ control
    🔡 check 🔤other control characters are written as \u00XX🔤 🧼🐇🧾 🛣 control❗️❗️ 🔤"/\u0001\u001f"🔤❗️

    💭 Objects and arrays
    🆕🧾❗️ ➡️ todo
    🔢 todo 🔤id🔤 1❗️
    🔡 todo 🔤title🔤 🔤Ship "it"🔤❗️
    👌 todo 🔤done🔤 👎❗️
    👌 todo 🔤urgent🔤 👍❗️
    🧩 todo 🔤tags🔤 📚🐇🧾 🍿 🧼🐇🧾 🔤a🔤❗️ 🧼🐇🧾 🔤b🔤❗️ 🍆❗️❗️
    🔡 check 🔤fields are written in the order they were added🔤 📤 todo❗️ 🔤{"id":1,"title":"Ship \"it\"","done":false,"urgent":true,"tags":["a","b"]}🔤❗️
    🔡 check 🔤an object without fields is {}🔤 📤 🆕🧾❗️❗️ 🔤{}🔤❗️
    🔡 check 🔤an array without items is []🔤 📚🐇🧾 🆕🍨🐚🔡🍆❗️❗️ 🔤[]🔤❗️
